// reader's numbers for wide groups are checked in t_k_vnni_layout.

body:
**[comments] Rule 2, restates identifiers: shorten**

"This case instantiates apply_page_tok ... (query 0 is hardware-visible and not software-required, so the call scores nothing). It is a compile check first." restates the test name ("compiles for 32 query heads on one 128-dimension K/V head") and the inline comment at 3756-3758, which explains the mask where it is built. The requirement, why this shape, and where the numbers are checked stay.

Proposed:
```cpp
// Software attention must stay available for every accepted geometry, also
// with TRON_K_VNNI. A 128-dimension K/V head shared by 32 query heads is such
// a geometry: the AMX kernel does not take it (its group is 4 heads), and the
// VNNI reader scores it in passes of 16 heads (k_vnni::qk_group). The
// reader's numbers for wide groups are checked in t_k_vnni_layout.
```

Line-to-code mapping (Rule 4):
L1-2 (software attention also with TRON_K_VNNI) -> the [k_vnni] tag and the two builds the case runs in; L2-4 (32 heads on one 128-dimension head: AMX group is 4, qk_group splits at 16) -> head_size / n_heads / n_kv_heads (3704-3706) and the static_assert (3709); L4-5 (numbers checked in t_k_vnni_layout) -> the REQUIREs at 3772-3773 check counts only.
